sk/skill/task_clarify.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_pursue.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/review-open-work.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/review.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/config.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/launch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/process.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/wave_home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/flowloop/wave.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ask.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/list.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/runs.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ssh.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/util.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/work.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/ask.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/ask_comments.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/child.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/project/answer.rs","rust/loopflow/src/project/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/project/runner.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/durable_ask_invocations__ef354215067cff23930e3c3adc5426c4.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/human_flow_positions__6f5c5c4049b353f3a1d7ad79c7b1c40f.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/task/runner.rs","rust/loopflow/src/task/runner/shipping_lifecycle_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/wave/playhead.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/config_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","swift/Loopflow/Models/AskAttentionRecord.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/AskExchangeRecord.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/LaunchTarget.swift","swift/Loopflow/Services/RegistryQuery.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/PodiumModel.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Services/Ghostty/GhosttyTerminalView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/AskAttentionView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/PodiumView.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/DTOFixtureTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/LocalWaveAgentLauncherTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/PodiumModelTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/RegistryQueryTests.swift","swift/README.md","tests/fixtures/dto/ask_attention.json","tests/fixtures/dto/ask_exchange.json","tests/fixtures/dto/turn.json","tests/goldens/basic.md","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_review_slice.md","tests/goldens/with_direction.md"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1166,"title":"usage: unify live provider accounting","body":"## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf usage\nlf usage --json | jq '.windows, .readings[0]'\nlf ps --sort rate\nlf top\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR replaces completed-turn spend snapshots and per-surface rate math with one provider-usage pipeline. Claude and Codex emit cumulative checkpoints during each Turn, SQLite stores provisional and final receipts, and Rust derives a fixed-window `UsageSnapshot`. CLI and Mac surfaces now agree on live output, cache, reasoning, cost, context pressure, and Work attribution without double-counting or treating missing measurements as zero.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added 5-second, 5-minute, 1-hour, and 24-hour usage rollups across global, repository, Wave, Project, Task, Exec, and Invocation scopes\n- Moved provider receipts into a dedicated checkpoint ledger, including migration and backfill of existing Turn usage\n- Routed headless Codex launches through the app-server harness to preserve session identity and stream usage consistently\n- Embedded the canonical snapshot in `lf ps` and `lf top`, and expanded `lf usage` token, cache, reasoning, and cost reporting\n- Updated the Mac Podium and telemetry dashboard to consume the same snapshot and refresh live activity every two seconds\n- Aligned documentation, DTO fixtures, and PR workflow tests with the app-server and usage model","files":[],"additions":3705,"deletions":1589,"changed_files":74,"merge_commit":"3c59a7f68f66ca20a002bd627f4a3c0bfb56fd45"},{"number":1175,"title":"ask: make blocking interventions durable","body":"## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf ask --user \"Choose the proof\"\nlf ask list --user\nlf ask open ask_...\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaces turn-local Ask/Answer exchanges with durable Ask sessions that survive provider, shell, and presentation loss. CLI flows, headless human gates, and Loopflow.app now share one authorized lifecycle for claiming, presenting, resolving, declining, releasing, escalating, or cancelling an intervention without consuming turns while work waits.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added explicit Ask origins, targets, states, typed results, active Invocation ownership, and exact presentation fences\n- Made `human: true` flow nodes durable Ask steps while direct TTY invocations remain human-present\n- Added the User-attention queue and embedded Ghostty/external-terminal Ask presentation to the Mac app\n- Added `lf ask` queue/session commands and `lf --as task|project|wave:...` for running a skill as existing Work\n- Made bare `lf` open the terminal control conversation and kept the app under `lf desktop`\n- Added focused `design` and `launch-plan` flows for reviewing a design, retaining its core, and launching independent follow-up Tasks","files":[],"additions":9185,"deletions":3736,"changed_files":101,"merge_commit":"156623e476cfdbecc168ed21039e3eaece634c50"},{"number":1189,"title":"install: pin refresh before asset redirects","body":"## Summary\n\n- Resolve the latest GitHub Release tag before downloading any assets.\n- Download both SHA256SUMS and install.sh from that immutable tag.\n- Cover signed release-assets redirects so CDN URLs cannot be mistaken for release tags.\n\n## Verification\n\n- uv run pytest -q python/tests/test_install_script.py\n- uv run ruff check scripts/install.py python/tests/test_install_script.py\n- uv run ruff format --check scripts/install.py python/tests/test_install_script.py\n- live latest-release lookup resolves v0.12.7","files":[],"additions":24,"deletions":22,"changed_files":2,"merge_commit":"f04718d53fd9163c6f6f37ea23f6186f2fdabf2d"},{"number":1195,"title":"podium: replace wave score with a live console","body":"## Try it\n\n```bash\nswift run --package-path swift LoopflowMac\nswift test --package-path swift --filter FaderSwitchTests\nopen docs/reviews/podium-console-before-after/index.html\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaces the Podium’s permanent Wave Score sidebar with a path-based console that gives the selected work the full center surface. Temporary cascading drawers preserve Wave → Project → Task navigation, while a shared fader language combines runtime state, token output, and legal lifecycle controls.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a burgundy selection path with overlay drawers that retract after choosing a Task\n- Added faders whose color shows state, fill shows five-minute output, and press starts or stops Wave and Task agents through existing `lf` lifecycle commands\n- Added selection-specific Wave, Project, and Task surfaces while keeping the unselected view focused on cross-Wave NOW triage\n- Moved repository scope into the Podium bar and kept Activity synchronized with the selected node\n- Added focused signal and verb tests, updated Podium UI coverage, and included an interactive before-and-after review","files":[],"additions":2324,"deletions":637,"changed_files":10,"merge_commit":"4b432c060f9d7aaa8f42a66a8ebf5cf9c41f4fef"},{"number":1196,"title":"lf auth connect: finish browser handoff hands-free","body":"## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf auth connect claude\n```\n\nApprove the request in the browser. Login now completes automatically through the browser handoff; if the browser shows a one-time code instead, paste it into the terminal.\n\n## Summary\n\nImproves authorization-code provider connections so the normal browser callback and the terminal fallback work concurrently. This keeps the happy path hands-free while preserving a reliable recovery path when the browser cannot reach the local callback.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Waits for browser completion while accepting a pasted authorization code\n- Gives interactive OAuth flows up to ten minutes to finish\n- Exits promptly after browser completion without waiting on the backup stdin reader\n- Leaves providers without authorization-code input on their existing flow","files":[],"additions":70,"deletions":3,"changed_files":2,"merge_commit":"7123b25b11718b1d97ddac7339250c16a9b5e16f"},{"number":1197,"title":"discord: harden binding ownership and restart reconciliation","body":"## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf home id\ndoppler run -- lf wave <name>\ncargo test -p loopflow discord_chat\n```\n\nSet `chat.home_id` to the Wave’s placed Home before starting its Discord listener.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR prevents copied repositories and stale placement data from starting competing Discord listeners. A binding now starts only when its configured Home, durable Wave placement, and local Home agree, while preserving the process-held lease that excludes concurrent listeners on that Home. It also makes restart reconciliation distinguish repeated delivery parts so one confirmed provider echo cannot satisfy another identical part.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Validate Discord ownership and Wave placement before token or provider access\n- Parse chat configuration independently so malformed unrelated Wave policy does not block listener startup\n- Reject unknown Discord binding fields and retain typed `HomeId` values in ownership errors\n- Ignore already-confirmed provider messages when reconciling repeated delivery content\n- Document the portable ownership model and add focused regression coverage","files":[],"additions":214,"deletions":52,"changed_files":5,"merge_commit":"04bc44ceac3dce665ed9ddf0f2d67ce39a0ec980"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.7\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.7 makes a verified published release the single unit of production Home upgrades. The same rule now governs release automation itself: generated release state is rebuilt when its source frontier changes, never rebased into something that only looks current. Wave agents also preserve more reusable prompt context and expose whether that reuse is paying off.\n\n## Homes move between verified runtime generations\n\nProduction upgrades now activate a matched `lf`, `lfd`, Mac app, and schema generation from one pinned published release. The transition is durable and recoverable, so a Home cannot quietly split across source-built binaries, migrations, and application versions (#1186).\n\n- `refresh` pins the latest published tag, verifies the installer, native archive, and Mac app against published SHA-256 checksums, then upgrades through the external installation path.\n- The Home records each runtime generation, upgrade phase, affected Work, and generation-aware Run trigger before activation.\n- Upgrades fence new work, drain active Runs, advance migrations, activate the matched artifacts, restart the configured keeper, and reconcile enabled Waves, Projects, and Tasks.\n- Durable receipts and recovery guards let an interrupted transition resume or roll back instead of leaving mixed binaries and schemas active.\n- `lfd` health now exposes runtime identity, making the active generation observable after restart.\n- Source builds remain available for validation under `local-bin/`, but validation-only control-plane artifacts cannot be promoted into production.\n\n## Release recovery rebuilds stale generated state\n\nRelease preparation now treats its output as immutable relative to the main revision that produced it. If main advances, or an existing release PR is dirty or behind, Loopflow starts preparation again from current main rather than rebasing already-generated migrations, manifests, or notes (#1187).\n\n- Recovery fetches and verifies the exact remote release head before resetting controller-owned generated state.\n- A prepared head that is already integrated can finalize without another rebase; a head that falls behind is rebuilt through every preparation step.\n- Auto-merge is armed only for the observed exact head and can be re-armed safely if GitHub drops it.\n- Cron publishing keeps private Home topology out of repository output while preserving the configured provider authority needed for publish preflight.\n\nThis closes the recovery path that allowed v0.12.6 to publish artifacts containing draft migrations. Installed promotion correctly rejected those artifacts; v0.12.7 prevents release recovery from producing that state again.\n\n## Prompt reuse is higher and measurable\n\nWave prompts now place stable doctrine and goals ahead of frequently changing memory and wake content, increasing the prefix providers can reuse. Persisted OpenCode conversations also survive harness restarts when the stored session remains available, with a clean fallback when it does not (#1185).\n\n- `lf usage --cached --days 7` reports cache writes and prompt-cache hit percentage by repository and provider.\n- `lf usage --days 7 --json` includes cache-write tokens in the shared usage record.\n- Cache-write accounting now persists through SQLite and the shared Rust/Swift usage DTO.\n\n## Operational notes\n\nUse `uv run python scripts/install.py local` to build validation-only artifacts. Use `uv run python scripts/install.py refresh` to pin, verify, and activate the latest published generation on the active Home; direct source-build promotion is no longer the production upgrade path.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":1,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}